    "content": "Hofstra University is a private institution in Hempstead, New York, known for its 13 schools (including law and medicine), a 13:1 student-faculty ratio, and hosting presidential debates. Founded in 1935, it offers roughly 200 programs to ~10,000 students. The Hofstra Pride competes in NCAA Division I, with men's basketball recently appearing in the 2026 NCAA Tournament. Key Aspects of Hofstra University: Academics: Offers a variety of programs through the Frank G. Zarb School of Business, College of Liberal Arts and Sciences, and Maurice A. Dean School of Law, with ~93% of faculty holding the highest degree in their field. Location: Located 25 miles from New York City. Rankings: U.S. News & World Report ranks Hofstra #183 in National Universities and #99 in Best Value Schools for 2026. Athletics: 21 Division I teams, featuring men's basketball (2026 CAA champions), lacrosse, and wrestling, as detailed on the official athletics website and NCAA.com. Campus Life: Features 35 residence halls, 16 eateries, and 200+ student organizations. Notable Alumni: Includes Francis Ford Coppola, Speedy Claxton, and Christopher Walken. Recent News (March 2026): Men's Basketball: The Hofstra Pride competed in the 2026 NCAA Tournament, losing in the first round to Alabama. Events: The university recently held a Spring 2026 Graduation Fair and other campus events.",
